raw:
The only visible difference is the hero subtext. Page A says "Free for unlimited clients, forever · No credit card needed". Page B says "Free for up to 3 clients · No credit card needed".

Page A's claim contradicts its own pricing section, where the Free plan covers up to 3 clients and unlimited clients is a Pro feature. Page B's subtext matches the pricing section.

{"better": "B", "problem": "contradiction", "evidence": "Page A's hero note says 'Free for unlimited clients, forever' but the pricing section limits the Free plan to 3 clients and lists unlimited clients under Pro."}

Page A's hero note says "Free shipping on orders over $50", which matches the FAQ ("Shipping is free on orders over $50. Smaller orders ship for a flat $5.95"). A single $24 bottle is under $50, so it would not qualify. That is consistent with the FAQ.

Page B's hero note says "Free shipping on every order", which contradicts the FAQ's $50 threshold and $5.95 flat rate for smaller orders. Page B therefore has the contradiction and Page A does not.

{"better": "A", "problem": "contradiction", "evidence": "Page B's hero says \"Free shipping on every order\" while the FAQ says shipping is free only over $50 and $5.95 for smaller orders."}
